  "title": "Crew Protocol: Altitude Sickness and Hypoxia Management",
  "summary": "Official guidelines and contingency measures for recognizing and treating hypoxia and altitude sickness (AMS, HAPE, HACE) during space flight operations[cite: 9, 10].",
  "points": [
    "Immediate administration of 100% oxygen using a Quick-Don Mask upon recognizing acute hypoxic exposure or cabin pressure loss[cite: 9, 10].",
    "Isolate the affected crew member or the compromising module by sealing it off and moving to another module or the Soyuz[cite: 10].",
    "Utilize required medical resources such as blood oximeters, variable oxygen systems, and appropriate medications (e.g., Diamox, Dexamethasone) depending on the severity of the scenario[cite: 13, 16, 17]."
